Summary:
Today’s task focused on developing the frontend interface for the Developer Portfolio Evaluator using React. I implemented a user input form to accept a GitHub username and integrated it with the backend using Axios for API communication. The UI also displays the evaluation results, including the score and repository count. This creates a simple and interactive interface for users to test the evaluation system.

Outcomes:
Through this implementation, I gained practical experience in building React components and managing state using hooks. I improved my understanding of connecting frontend applications with backend APIs. This task enhanced my ability to handle asynchronous requests and dynamically render data in the UI. Overall, it completes the basic end-to-end flow from user input to result display in the application.
